cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  facetmark: measured multi-facet bookmark retrieval over a local SQLite
  library
message: >-
  If you use this software or its published measurements, please cite it using
  these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: 88lin
    website: 'https://github.com/88lin'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/88lin/facetmark'
url: 'https://github.com/88lin/facetmark'
abstract: >-
  facetmark indexes a personal bookmark library along four retrieval facets --
  lexical (FTS5 trigram and word-segment), content embeddings, model-generated
  intents filtered by a retrieve-back check, and save-session/graph context --
  fuses them with reciprocal rank fusion, and then measures whether each facet
  was worth adding. Every default ships from a pre-registered protocol with a
  criterion written before the measurement, and the negative results are
  published with the same prominence as the positive ones: four-facet fusion
  measured worse than the single content facet on 479 real queries, a gated
  context multiplier was shipped and then reverted after a targeted 361-query
  probe measured -18.83pp Recall@5 when the gate fires, the intent facet was
  demoted after a human read found only 38% of generated intents plausible, and
  a pre-registered karakeep round-trip returned roundtrip_unfaithful on
  list-level fidelity. The system runs entirely locally against a single SQLite
  file and never writes back to the browser's bookmark store.
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - bookmark management
  - reciprocal rank fusion
  - embeddings
  - evaluation
  - negative results
  - pre-registration
  - sqlite
  - karakeep
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-19'
